lvt provides CMake targets:

    find_package(lvt CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE lvt::core)

    # lvt locates its injectable TAP DLLs next to the binary it is linked into.
    # This copies them beside your executable:
    lvt_copy_tap_dlls(main)

Instead of lvt_copy_tap_dlls() you can call lvt::set_tap_directory() at runtime
or point the LVT_TAP_DIR environment variable at ${LVT_TOOLS_DIR}.

Headers are installed under include/lvt:

    #include <lvt/target.h>
    #include <lvt/tree_builder.h>
    #include <lvt/json_serializer.h>
    #include <lvt/lvt_config.h>   // which frameworks were compiled in

The WPF, WinForms and Avalonia providers additionally need a managed
tree-walker assembly, which cannot be built inside vcpkg because it requires
the .NET SDK and a NuGet restore. Those frameworks are detected and their
windows are walked, but managed enrichment is unavailable unless you deploy
LvtWpfTap.dll / LvtWinFormsTap.dll / LvtAvaloniaTreeWalker.dll alongside the
TAP DLLs yourself. Prebuilt copies ship in the GitHub releases at
https://github.com/asklar/lvt/releases.
